# nr-office-engine-transactions-batch: the transactions and the atomic batch of the office engine (modules mixdog-office::transactions and mixdog-office::batch)

Written without cargo: nothing below has been compiled (rustfmt parsed every file; the twin test replays a recording made by running the recorder
against C:/Project/mixdog). The modules are a library the Office tool's service (a later task of the office track) calls; this task registers no
protocol method and no service, so nothing is removed from SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After the modules the earlier fragments add (`session`, `snapshot`, `inspect`, `inline_audit`, `render`) add, and extend the crate documentation by one
line ("[`transactions`] begins, commits, rolls back and recovers a transaction from its journal; [`batch`] applies a list of operations to a session's
document all together or not at all."):

    pub mod batch;
    pub mod transactions;

The modules call `crate::session::mode::OfficeHost`, `crate::session::working_copy::{dirname, full_path, materialize_working_copy}` and
`crate::session::registry`; they need `pub mod mode; pub mod open; pub mod working_copy;` in session/mod.rs (nr-office-engine-open-create.wire).
They also call `mixdog_ooxml::portable::apply_portable_ooxml_batch` (nr-office-engine-open-create.wire adds `pub mod portable;` to mixdog-ooxml) and
`mixdog_office_pdf::batch::apply_batch` and `mixdog_office_pdf::content_ops::ContentOperations` (nr-office-pdf-content-ops.wire adds `pub mod batch;` and `pub mod content_ops;`).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
[dependencies], keeping the list sorted (`mixdog-fsio`, `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-office-base`, `mixdog-office-com`, `mixdog-office-design`, `mixdog-office-pdf`,
`mixdog-office-quality`, `mixdog-ooxml`, `mixdog-rt`, `mixdog-statefile`, `serde_json` are already there or added by the snapshot fragment):

    mixdog-xlsx-formula = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies], for the twin test (`mixdog-fonts`, `mixdog-pdf`, `tempfile`, `tokio` are already there):

    mixdog-raster = { workspace = true }

(`mixdog-xlsx-formula` is the engine that moves a filled formula; `mixdog-raster` gives the test an empty SVG font set for the PDF operation set. Both are
workspace members and [workspace.dependencies] entries; nothing of either depends on mixdog-office, so there is no cycle, and no external crate enters
the lock.)

## native/core/Cargo.lock
Package `mixdog-office`: add the dependencies mixdog-xlsx-formula and mixdog-raster (`cargo update -w` offline).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing by hand: no new external crate, no new feature. Run the hakari check after the manifest edit and take its output if it asks for a line.

