Add to `sets`, in name order (after "office-text-date" and the sets that sort between it and "office-transactions-batch"):

    { "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-transactions-batch.mjs --tree <tree>", "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-transactions-batch/MANIFEST.json", "manifestSha256": "4f5934c920ff23a338da5ab21822b6c0cb90b70194253eefe9b6c3519ae94e55",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-transactions-batch.mjs", "set": "office-transactions-batch", "totalBytes": 734310 }

(the fixture folder is not checked out in an engineer's worktree: native/core/fixtures/office-transactions-batch/{golden.json,MANIFEST.json} were written
at their paths by the recorder and added with `git add --sparse`; the set's MANIFEST.json records the identity of the tree it was recorded against as
"closest commit, not exact": the tree C:/Project/mixdog has uncommitted changes. The recording is deterministic apart from what the scrub names (the
temporary folders, the random parts of a checkpoint's name, the transaction ids); no program or window is involved: the Microsoft Office host is a script.)

## Interface the tool layer calls (crate mixdog-office)
`mixdog_office::transactions` (the future is not `Send`: drive it on the lane thread, as the snapshot's):
- `TransactionContext<'a, L: WriteLane, H> { snapshot: &SnapshotContext<InLane<L>, H>, note: &dyn WriteNote, registry: &Registry, env: &design::library::Environment }`
  (`env.now_ms` is `Date.now()`, so the journal's times are the product's clock). `H: ComHost` for the calls below, and `ComHost + OfficeHost` for recover.
- `begin_transaction`, `commit_transaction`, `rollback_transaction(&cx, &SessionHandle) -> Result<Value, TransactionError>`: `office_tx_<16 hex>`, the
  checkpoint in the temporary folder (`mixdog-office-transaction-<session>-<token><ext>`), the journal at `<data dir>/office-transactions/<id>.json` before
  any edit, the phases `committing` and `rolling_back` on disk before the work they name; rollback restores through the write note and verifies, failing
  with the remaining diff in the message. `TransactionError::Conflict(OfficeConflictError)` carries Node's `transaction_conflict` details (answer them as
  the result of the call); `TransactionError::Failed(String)` is a message.
- `recover_office_transaction(&cx, &args, data_dir)` (`args.transaction`, `args.strategy` = commit | rollback | discard; a recovered session is rebuilt from
  the journal and indexed in the registry, an Office session is re-attached through `OfficeHost::open_session`, a live document that is no longer open is
  answered with `live_document_not_open`), `pending_office_transactions(&cx, data_dir)` (the `transactions` listing, 30-day cleanup included).
- `capture_session_state`, `assert_transaction_unchanged`, `persist_office_transaction(&cx, &handle, phase)`, `transaction_document_diff`,
  `record_transaction_operations`, `transaction_view`, and `documents::{diff_documents, diff, operation_document_paths, operation_change_kind,
  document_snapshot_fingerprint}` (the diff holds at most 500 entries; `DIFF_LIMIT`).

`mixdog_office::batch`:
- `BatchContext<'a, L: WriteLane, H, B: BatchHost> { inspect: &InspectContext<L, H>, note, registry, env, host: &B }` and
  `apply_batch(&cx, &SessionHandle, &args) -> Result<Value, TransactionError>` (`applyBatch`): the trust gate, the working copy, the journal's `applying`
  mark, the backup (`<target>.mixdog-backup-<uuid>`, or the Office save-copy checkpoint for `import_slides`), the backend (Microsoft Office, portable OOXML,
  PDF, delimited file), the no-change check, the restore on error, and on success the snapshot version, the design state, the transaction's expected
  fingerprint and the inline audit. The backup and the scratch folders are always removed.
- `BatchHost` is what the service gives the batch beyond the lane: `pdf_operations(data_dir, cancel) -> ContentOperations` (the OCR context and the fonts of
  the process), `chart_picture(block, width, pdf) -> Future<Result<String, String>>` (the Word chart as a picture: `create_chart_pdf` with the process's
  `FontEnv`, then `render_pdf_pages` of page 1 at `Math.round(width * 3)` pixels wide and `maximum_scale` 3; answers the picture's path beside the PDF) and
  `brief_readings() -> &dyn BriefReadings` (the author crate's brief parser and readings).
- `prepare_batch_operations`, `with_shared_chart_defaults` (the COM batch's palette and particle defaults) are public for the Office host's own callers.
- `office-recalculation.mjs` is not ported a second time: `mixdog_office::render::recalculate_for_review` (nr-office-engine-render) is it, and the batch
  never calls it.

## Findings in files other tasks own (not touched here)
- `mixdog-office/src/session/working_copy.rs` calls `registry.retarget(env, handle, target)`, which `session/registry.rs` does not define (the sessions
  task owns both): `materialize_working_copy` does not compile until the registry has it. `retarget` is `release` of the old path and `index` of the new one
  with `session.target` replaced.
- `mixdog-office/src/tabular.rs` reports the file it writes to the write note in `apply_batch`; Node's `applyTabularBatch` does not (its caller does). The twin
  accepts the extra report for csv and tsv only.
